# shadcn/ui Component Library Standards

This project uses **shadcn/ui** as the **EXCLUSIVE** UI component library. No exceptions.

## Absolute Requirements

- **ONLY shadcn/ui components may be used for ALL UI in this project — no exceptions**
- **NEVER create custom UI components from scratch** — if a shadcn/ui component exists for the use case, use it
- **NEVER write custom CSS classes, inline styles, or styled components** for UI elements that shadcn/ui already covers
- If a shadcn/ui component does not exist for a specific need, extend or compose existing shadcn/ui components rather than building custom alternatives
- These rules apply to every file in the project, without exception
- This project is in dark mode so make sure there are no dark colored text on dark backgrounds (and vice versa)

## Clerk Authentication UI

- **ALL Clerk sign-in and sign-up buttons must use the shadcn/ui `<Button>` component** — never use Clerk's default button styling or custom button markup
- **Clerk sign-in and sign-up flows must be launched via a modal** — use Clerk's `modal` mode (not redirect mode) so authentication appears in an overlay without navigating away from the current page
- Configure Clerk's `<SignInButton>` and `<SignUpButton>` with `mode="modal"` and wrap them in the shadcn/ui `<Button>` component:

```tsx
import { SignInButton, SignUpButton } from "@clerk/nextjs";
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";

// Correct: shadcn/ui Button + Clerk modal mode
<SignInButton mode="modal">
  <Button>Sign In</Button>
</SignInButton>

<SignUpButton mode="modal">
  <Button>Sign Up</Button>
</SignUpButton>
```

- **NEVER** render Clerk's `<SignIn>` or `<SignUp>` components as full-page embedded forms — always use modal mode
- **NEVER** use raw `<button>` or `<a>` tags as Clerk trigger elements — always wrap with the shadcn/ui `<Button>`

## Initialization

If shadcn/ui is not initialized in the project, use the following command:

```bash
npx shadcn@latest init
```

## Component Installation

If a particular component is not installed, use the following command pattern:

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add [component-name]
```

**Example:** To install the button component:
```bash
npx shadcn@latest add button
```

## Prohibited Patterns

### ❌ DON'T: Create custom button or UI elements
```tsx
// Wrong - custom button markup
<button className="bg-blue-500 text-white px-4 py-2 rounded">Click me</button>

// Wrong - custom styled div acting as a button
<div onClick={handleClick} className="cursor-pointer ...">Click me</div>
```

### ❌ DON'T: Use Clerk buttons without shadcn/ui wrapper
```tsx
// Wrong - raw Clerk button with no shadcn/ui Button
<SignInButton mode="modal" />

// Wrong - redirect mode instead of modal
<SignInButton mode="redirect">
  <Button>Sign In</Button>
</SignInButton>
```

### ✅ DO: Always use shadcn/ui components
```tsx
// Correct - shadcn/ui Button
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";
<Button variant="default">Click me</Button>

// Correct - Clerk modal with shadcn/ui Button
<SignInButton mode="modal">
  <Button variant="outline">Sign In</Button>
</SignInButton>
```

## Common Components

Some frequently used shadcn/ui components include:
- `button` - Interactive buttons (required for ALL clickable elements)
- `card` - Content containers
- `input` - Form inputs
- `dialog` - Modal dialogs
- `toast` - Notification toasts
- `dropdown-menu` - Dropdown menus
- `select` - Select dropdowns
- `checkbox` - Checkboxes
- `radio-group` - Radio button groups
- `tabs` - Tab navigation
